<title>FINLAND: FINNISH JAN WOOD PURCHASES DOWN 16 PCT YR/YR-METLA.</title>
<headline>FINNISH JAN WOOD PURCHASES DOWN 16 PCT YR/YR-METLA.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The forest industry's timber purchases from private forests fell 16 percent year-on-year in January to 2.2 million cubic metres, the Finnish Forest Research Institute (METLA) said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>The amount was 1.1 million cubic metres down on December 1996, it said.</p>
<p>&quot;Despite the lack of a contract in the timber trade, timber purchases from private forests in January matched the level of previous years,&quot; METLA said, adding that January purchases in 1994-1996 were between 2.0 and 2.7 million cubic metres.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0248</p>
</text>
